# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the ctest suite (used only when built with -fsanitize=address).
# One-time initialisation allocations inside NVIDIA's user-space libraries (cuInit, NGX runtime,
# the VFX SDK) are reported at process exit: ~70 KB per process, none allocated by libnvvsr.
# Known limit: a leak whose stack passes through one of these libraries is also hidden, e.g. an
# SDK object we forgot to destroy; the VRAM/RSS growth checks in test_stress cover that case.
# NVIDIA runtime code unpacked into memfd files (shows as /proc/self/fd/N): the SDK leaks per model load.
leak:/proc/self/fd/
leak:libcuda.so
leak:libnvidia-ngx
leak:libnvngxruntime
leak:libVideoFX
leak:libnvVFX
leak:libNVCVImage
